    move: gen_store_fixture.py's docstring described the Go reader as
    ORDER BY rowid long after store/sqlite.go moved to ORDER BY ts, id (§6.2).
    
    Residue swept in the same change — README layout + run sections, FINDINGS
    method artifacts + regenerate block, the decode.go conformance-contract
    comment, and the four "run: python3 tools/…" hints in the test failure
    messages. tools/README.md is left as the pointer. SPEC.md's conformance
    appendix rides the next commit, where the same hunk also registers the new
    fixture.
    
    NOT swept: the "generated_by" strings inside the already-committed
    testdata/**.json. Those record where those bytes actually came from;
    rewriting a provenance field without regenerating the artifact would be a
    false claim. The next regeneration updates them on its own. Noted in
    tools/README.md.
    
